---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Nav from '../components/Nav.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';

const lastUpdated = 'September 25, 2026';
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy Policy — HebrewEdu"
  description="Privacy Policy for the HebrewEdu app and website."
>
  <Nav />
  <main class="legal-page">
    <div class="container legal-container">
      <div class="legal-header">
        <p class="eyebrow">Legal</p>
        <h1 class="display-lg mt-xs">Privacy Policy</h1>
        <p class="lead mt-sm">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>
      </div>

      <article class="legal-content">
        <section>
          <h2>Introduction</h2>
          <p>Learn Hebrew – Read & Speak (also referred to as HebrewEdu or AlefBet Tutor), developed by VIKTOR SOKOLIUK ("we", "our", or "us"), respects your privacy. This Privacy Policy describes how information is handled when you use our mobile application distributed through Google Play and the Apple App Store. Practices may differ depending on the platform and app version.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>1. Information We Handle</h2>
          <p>The App does not require an account, login, or social login. We do not intentionally ask you to provide your name, email address, or other profile information in the current app. Local app preferences and learning state may be stored on your device where applicable and are not shared with other users by us.</p>
          <p>The App communicates with the HebrewEdu backend to retrieve educational and app data. When these services are used, technical and network information necessary to provide, secure, and troubleshoot the service may be processed by the relevant service providers.</p>
          <p>Both the Android and iOS apps use Firebase, a third-party service provided by Google. On Android, Firebase may be used for functions such as crash reporting or remote configuration. On iOS, the App uses Firebase Core and Cloud Functions. Firebase may process information in accordance with <a href="https://firebase.google.com/support/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Firebase's Privacy Policy</a>.</p>
          <p>Where the word-explanation feature is available, when you request an explanation, the word or text you submit and technical request data (such as IP address and request identifiers) are sent to a Firebase Cloud Function, which uses the OpenAI API to generate the explanation. OpenAI processes the request text as a service provider under its API terms and policies. We do not send account data or anything that identifies you by name. Please do not include personal information in text you submit.</p>
          <p>For Premium subscriptions, RevenueCat is used as a third-party subscription-management service to support entitlement status and restoration. Depending on the platform and transaction, RevenueCat may process purchase or subscription status, app-specific identifiers and technical information, and related transaction information necessary for these functions. RevenueCat does not receive payment-card details from us. Apple or Google Play handles payment credentials and store billing for purchases made through its store.</p>
          <p>The current iOS app does not request access to location, camera, microphone, contacts, calendar, Bluetooth, motion, speech recognition, or pasteboard data.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>2. Advertising (Google AdMob)</h2>
          <p>The free version of the App shows Google AdMob rewarded ads only — no banner or interstitial ads. Ads are opt-in: an ad is shown only when you tap "Watch ad" to receive a reward, such as extra daily attempts, extra quiz retries, or in-app coins. Premium subscribers are not shown ads; on iOS, the ads SDK is not started for verified Premium users.</p>
          <p>When ads are requested or shown, Google may process device and advertising identifiers (such as IDFA, IDFV, or the Android Advertising ID), IP address, approximate location derived from IP address, and ad interaction and diagnostic data. This information is used to serve and measure ads, limit how often ads are shown, prevent fraud, and personalize ads where you have consented. Learn more in <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites" target="_blank" rel="noopener">How Google uses information from sites or apps that use its services</a> and <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Google's Privacy Policy</a>.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>3. Consent and Your Privacy Choices</h2>
          <p>The App uses Google's User Messaging Platform (UMP) to manage advertising consent. If you are in the European Economic Area (EEA), the United Kingdom, or Switzerland, you will see a consent form before any ad is requested. If you decline consent, only non-personalized ads may be shown.</p>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>iOS:</strong> You can change your choice at any time via the "Privacy choices" link at the bottom of the Premium screen.</li>
            <li><strong>Android:</strong> There is currently no in-app setting for this. You can change your choice by clearing the App's data, by reinstalling the App, or by contacting us.</li>
          </ul>
          <p><strong>App Tracking Transparency (iOS):</strong> The iOS app may ask for your permission to track. If you decline, or if you are not asked, the advertising identifier (IDFA) is not accessed and ads may be less personalized. You can change tracking permission at any time in iOS Settings.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>4. Data Retention and Security</h2>
          <p>Local preferences and learning data remain on your device until you delete them, remove the App, or the App changes how that data is stored. Information processed by backend, subscription, advertising, AI, or store providers is retained according to the providers' practices and as needed to provide, secure, and administer their services. We use reasonable measures intended to protect information, but no method of storage or transmission is completely secure.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>5. Children's Privacy</h2>
          <p>The App is not directed to children under 13, and we do not knowingly collect personal information from children under 13. If we become aware that such information was provided to us, we will take reasonable steps to delete it promptly.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>6. Data Deletion Rights</h2>
          <p>You have the right to request access to, correction of, or deletion of personal data that we control, subject to applicable law. Because the App does not require an account and much of its learning data is stored locally, you can also remove local data by deleting the App or using available device/app controls. To make a request, please contact us via email: <a href="mailto:vicsothemes@gmail.com">vicsothemes@gmail.com</a></p>
          <p>We will respond as soon as possible and act in accordance with applicable data protection laws.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>7. Users in the EEA and UK (GDPR)</h2>
          <p>If you are in the European Economic Area or the United Kingdom, the following applies in addition to the rest of this Policy.</p>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Controller:</strong> VIKTOR SOKOLIUK, <a href="mailto:vicsothemes@gmail.com">vicsothemes@gmail.com</a>.</li>
            <li><strong>Legal bases:</strong> performance of a contract (providing the App and Premium); consent (personalized advertising); legitimate interests (security, fraud prevention, non-personalized ads, and providing word explanations you request).</li>
            <li><strong>Your rights:</strong> you may request access, rectification, erasure, restriction of processing, objection to processing, and data portability, and you may withdraw consent at any time without affecting processing carried out before withdrawal. Contact us by email to exercise these rights.</li>
            <li><strong>Complaints:</strong> you have the right to lodge a complaint with a data protection supervisory authority, in particular in the country where you live or work.</li>
            <li><strong>International transfers:</strong> our service providers (Google, including Firebase and AdMob; OpenAI; and RevenueCat) may process information outside your country under the safeguards they provide for such transfers.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>8. External Services and Links</h2>
          <p>The App may rely on the following services as described above. Their handling of information is governed by their own terms and privacy policies:</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Apple (App Store and in-app purchases on iOS)</li>
            <li>Google Play (distribution and in-app purchases on Android)</li>
            <li>Firebase — <a href="https://firebase.google.com/support/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Privacy and Security in Firebase</a></li>
            <li>Google AdMob and User Messaging Platform — <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Google Privacy Policy</a></li>
            <li>OpenAI (word explanations) — <a href="https://openai.com/policies/privacy-policy" target="_blank" rel="noopener">OpenAI Privacy Policy</a></li>
            <li>RevenueCat (subscription management)</li>
            <li>The HebrewEdu backend</li>
          </ul>
          <p>If we provide a link to an external website, review that site's privacy policy before providing information.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>9. Changes to This Policy</h2>
          <p>We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. Any significant changes will be reflected in the app or posted through an updated document. We recommend reviewing this page occasionally to stay informed of updates.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>10. Contact Us</h2>
          <p>If you have any questions or concerns about this Privacy Policy, feel free to reach out:</p>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Developer:</strong> VIKTOR SOKOLIUK</li>
            <li><strong>Email:</strong> <a href="mailto:vicsothemes@gmail.com">vicsothemes@gmail.com</a></li>
          </ul>
          <p>Thank you for using Learn Hebrew – Read & Speak!</p>
        </section>
      </article>
    </div>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Layout>

<style>
.legal-page { background: #f8f8f6; }

.legal-container {
  max-width: var(--w-narrow);
  padding-block: var(--space-xl) var(--space-2xl);
}

.legal-header {
  padding-bottom: var(--space-lg);
  border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
  margin-bottom: var(--space-lg);
}

.legal-content { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 2rem; }

.legal-content section h2 {
  font-family: var(--font-display);
  font-size: 1.125rem;
  font-weight: 700;
  color: var(--ink);
  margin-bottom: 0.625rem;
}

.legal-content p, .legal-content li {
  font-size: 0.9375rem;
  color: var(--ink-light);
  line-height: 1.75;
}

.legal-content ul {
  padding-left: 1.25rem;
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  gap: 0.375rem;
  margin-top: 0.5rem;
}

.legal-content strong { color: var(--ink-mid); }
.legal-content a { color: var(--brand); text-decoration: underline; }

/* Сброс глобального section { padding-block } */
.legal-content section { padding-block: 0; }
</style>
